# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 misc.cc giac_hamdist (under _hamdist, two integers and the binop list forms; G791, backlog F476): in the mixed cases (_INT___ZINT and _ZINT__INT_) the small integer was set with mpz_set_ui, which reads a negative int as 2^32+v (hamdist(-1,2^40) = 33, hamdist(-1,-2^40) = 4294967295, right 40), and two integers of opposite signs gave a count: mpz_hamdist returns the largest bit count (hamdist(-2^40,2^40) = 4294967295) and the two-small-integers loop counts 31 bits (hamdist(-1,2) = 30, hamdist(3,-5) = 28). Their Hamming distance in two's complement (unbounded, as GMP and Python read it) is infinite, so they are now refused (hamdist: the integers have opposite signs), and the mixed cases use mpz_set_si, as patch 0062 did for bitand, bitor and bitxor. Two integers of the same sign keep their count (hamdist(-1,-2) = 1, hamdist(1,2^40) = 2); the vector and string forms are unchanged.
